Install` expo-maps` in a development build, then render` AppleMaps.View` on iOS and` GoogleMaps.View` on Android. Both components take the same camera, marker and location data, so one wrapper covers both platforms.


Most map tutorials for React Native are written for` react-native-maps` , so their props don’t carry over to Expo’s library. Copy a` <MapView>` snippet into an expo-maps project and you get type errors on everything, including the camera.


This guide covers the whole flow in expo-maps: picking the library, building the app, adding the Android API key, rendering a map on both platforms, adding markers, centring on the user and handling marker taps. It also covers the iOS version limits that decide which features you can use. If you want vector tiles and custom styles from Mapbox instead, see[creating a React Native map with Mapbox](https://blog.openreplay.com/create-a-react-native-map-using-mapbox/) .


## Key Takeaways


- expo-maps shows Apple Maps on iOS and Google Maps on Android through two components,` AppleMaps.View` and` GoogleMaps.View` , and it does not support Google Maps on iOS.
- Run expo-maps in a development build. Apple Maps needs no API key, but Android needs a Google Maps key at` android.config.googleMaps.apiKey` in app.json, followed by a rebuild.
- ` cameraPosition` only sets where the map starts. To move the camera later, call` setCameraPosition` on a ref to the map.
- Expo’s docs list iOS 17 as the minimum for expo-maps, and marker tap callbacks such as` onMarkerClick` need iOS 18.


## Should You Use expo-maps or react-native-maps?


For an Expo project that already uses development builds, choose expo-maps. Choose` react-native-maps` if you need Google Maps on iOS or need to run inside Expo Go.[expo-maps](https://expo.dev/blog/introducing-expo-maps-a-modern-maps-api-for-expo-developers) is Expo’s own maps library, and it renders through SwiftUI on iOS and Jetpack Compose on Android.[react-native-maps](https://github.com/react-native-maps/react-native-maps) is community-maintained and gives you one` MapView` API that works with several map providers.


